# {{.ServerName}}

An MCP server that lets Claude control **{{.Name}}** through the device's own
web API. [har2mcp](https://github.com/donaldsteele/har2mcp) generated it from
a recording of the device's web UI.

It runs on your machine, talks to the device over HTTP, and speaks MCP over
stdio. Your password stays in your environment; it is not in this code.

## Build

You need Go 1.26 or later.

```sh
go mod tidy                # only if go.sum is missing
go build -o {{.BinaryName}} .
```

On Windows, build `{{.BinaryName}}.exe` instead: `go build -o {{.BinaryName}}.exe .`

## Configure

The server reads these environment variables:

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_URL` | The device's address, such as `{{.ExampleURL}}`. Only the scheme, host and port are used.{{if .BaseURL}} Defaults to `{{.BaseURL}}`, the address in the recording.{{end}} |
{{- if ne .Mode "none"}}
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_USER` | The user name you log in to the device with. |
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_PASSWORD` | That user's password. |
{{- end}}
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_INSECURE` | Set to `1` to accept a self-signed TLS certificate. |
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_FILES_DIR` | The only folder that upload and download tools may read or write. Defaults to `{{.FilesDirDefault}}`, created on first use. |
{{- if .Browser}}
| `{{.EnvPrefix}}_BROWSER` | Path to Chrome, Chromium or Edge, if the server can't find it. |
{{- end}}

## Register with Claude Code

```sh
claude mcp add --transport stdio \
  --env {{.EnvPrefix}}_URL={{.ExampleURL}} \
{{- if ne .Mode "none"}}
  --env {{.EnvPrefix}}_USER=your-user \
  --env {{.EnvPrefix}}_PASSWORD='your-password' \
{{- end}}
  {{.Name}} -- /path/to/{{.BinaryName}}
```

## Register with Claude Desktop

Add this to `claude_desktop_config.json` (Settings > Developer > Edit Config),
then restart Claude Desktop:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{.Name}}": {
      "command": "/path/to/{{.BinaryName}}",
      "env": {
        "{{.EnvPrefix}}_URL": "{{.ExampleURL}}"{{if ne .Mode "none"}},
        "{{.EnvPrefix}}_USER": "your-user",
        "{{.EnvPrefix}}_PASSWORD": "your-password"{{end}}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

On Windows, use the full path to `{{.BinaryName}}.exe` with doubled
backslashes, such as `"C:\\Tools\\{{.BinaryName}}.exe"`.

## Logging in

{{if eq .Mode "http" -}}
The server logs in on the first tool call by replaying the recorded login
request with your user name and password, keeps the session cookie, and logs
in again when the session expires.
{{- else if eq .Mode "browser" -}}
The device's login page scrambles the password before sending it, so the
server logs in the way you do: it opens the login page in headless Chrome,
types your user name and password, and keeps the session cookies. It logs in
again when the session expires.

**Chrome, Chromium or Edge must be installed on the machine that runs this
server.** Set `{{.EnvPrefix}}_BROWSER` if it is not in a standard location.
{{- else if eq .Mode "basic" -}}
The device uses HTTP Basic authentication: the server sends your user name
and password with every request. There is no login request and no session
to keep.
{{- else -}}
The recording had no login, so the server sends requests without one.
{{- end}}
{{- if or (eq .Mode "http") (eq .Mode "browser")}}

After a failed login the server waits 15 minutes before it tries again (30
seconds after a network error), so a wrong password can't trip the device's
lockout, which on many devices also locks you out of the web page. Fix the
password and restart the server.
{{- end}}

